# Solidity Documentation Standards

<version>1.0.0</version>

## Context
- Applies to all Solidity smart contracts
- Balances detailed technical documentation with readability
- Preserves critical implementation details while avoiding verbosity

## Requirements

1. Documentation Format
   - Use multi-line format `/** */` for all NatSpec comments
   - Maintain consistent indentation within comment blocks
   - Use `@inheritdoc` for interface implementations when appropriate

2. Contract-Level Documentation
   - Title and author
   - One-line notice explaining core functionality
   - Brief dev notes for key technical details
   - No tutorial-style explanations

3. Function Documentation
   - External/public: document parameters, return values, and key behaviors
   - Internal/private: focus on implementation details and edge cases
   - Keep implementation notes focused on non-obvious technical aspects

4. Complex Mechanism Documentation
   - Document in numbered sections
   - Include purpose, parameters, mechanism, integration
   - Focus on technical implementation rather than usage guides
   - Place in relevant contract section

## Examples

<example>
/** 
 * @dev Top-Up Mechanism Design:
 *
 * 1. Purpose:
 *    - Maintains minimum bonded balance
 *    - Prevents operational disruption
 *
 * 2. Parameters:
 *    - minBonded: Minimum balance threshold
 *    - maxTopUpPerPeriod: Auto-bonding limit
 *
 * 3. Integration:
 *    - Triggered in _spendFromBonded
 *    - Configurable via setMinBondedBalance
 */
</example>

<example type="invalid">
/**
 * @dev Top-Up System
 *
 * This system helps users manage their bonded balance by automatically
 * topping up when needed. Users can configure various settings to control
 * how the system behaves. When a user's balance gets low, the system will
 * automatically add more tokens from their unbonded balance.
 *
 * To use this system, first call setMinBondedBalance with your desired
 * parameters. The system will then monitor your balance and...
 */
</example>

<critical>
- Documentation MUST focus on technical implementation, not usage guides
- Complex mechanisms require structured sections but remain concise
- Preserve all critical technical details while removing tutorial content
</critical>